*__pycache__*

node_modules

*.env


# Agent trace recorder output. Full payloads: balances, positions and the
# user's own messages. Diagnostics, never committed.
traces/

# Local database dumps (make db-dump). Full copies of the live DB: credentials
# hashes, balances, chat history. Backups and hand-offs, never commits --
# `seeds/` is the reviewable, per-user thing that IS committed.
dumps/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: junit.xml, coverage.xml and frontend/coverage/
# are tracked because CLAUDE.md and README name them as the evidence for the
# 100% requirement. Listing them here would be a no-op anyway -- .gitignore
# does not apply to files git already tracks.
#
# The cost is that every one of them conflicts on every merge (17 of the 23
# conflicts in this one). They are regenerated by running the suites, so the
# resolution is always "re-run the tests", never "hand-merge the XML".
# Untracking them and publishing them as CI artifacts instead is a team call.
